    LineComment "// The operator contracts: the prelude gathers the comparison and"
    Newline "\n"
    LineComment "// arithmetic operators into named interfaces — comparable (== !=), orderable"
    Newline "\n"
    LineComment "// (< <= > >=), and numeric (unary +, and + - * / %) — that the builtin types opt"
    Newline "\n"
    LineComment "// into at their own definition sites. A generic function can then bound a type"
    Newline "\n"
    LineComment "// parameter by the contract rather than by a concrete type, so one definition"
    Newline "\n"
    LineComment "// works over every builtin that carries those operators: the bound names the"
    Newline "\n"
    LineComment "// methods, and the call folds with the concrete type, no runtime dispatch."
    Newline "\n"
    Newline "\n"
    LineComment "// orderable is a bound: max may call a.gteq(b) because every type satisfying the"
    Newline "\n"
    LineComment "// bound carries the >= operator. int and string both impl orderable."
    Newline "\n"
    DocComment "/// The larger of two orderable values."
    Newline "\n"
